      "id": "emergent_ai_governance_crisis",
      "description": "As public sentiment collapses and multiple member states bypass EU coordination to secure AI access through bilateral deals, a coalition of central European states formally proposes an emergency restructuring of the Union's AI governance framework, arguing that the current paralysis risks irreversible fragmentation. The proposal demands delegation of sovereign compute access decisions to a new intergovernmental body outside the normal legislative process.",
